faqs:
  - q: "Will automated emails hurt my deliverability?"
    a: "Not when done correctly. We set up proper email authentication (SPF, DKIM, DMARC), warm up your sending domain gradually, and use engagement-based sending that prioritizes active subscribers. Our sequences are designed to provide genuine value — not spam. This keeps open rates high and spam complaints near zero."
  - q: "How long does it take to set up marketing automation?"
    a: "A basic automation system with a welcome sequence, follow-up campaign, and lead nurturing flow takes about 1-2 weeks to set up. More complex systems with multiple triggers, segmentation, and conditional logic take 3-4 weeks. We write all the copy, design the templates, and configure the workflows — you just approve and launch."
  - q: "What gets automated exactly?"
    a: "The most common automations we build include: welcome email series when someone fills out a form, follow-up sequences after consultations or quotes, appointment reminders and post-visit check-ins, review request campaigns, re-engagement campaigns for inactive leads, birthday or anniversary emails, and referral requests after completed projects."
  - q: "Do I still need to do any manual marketing?"
    a: "Automation handles the repetitive, time-sensitive follow-ups that most businesses forget to do. You should still create original content, engage on social media, and have personal conversations with high-value prospects. Think of automation as your marketing assistant that handles the routine work so you can focus on the creative and personal touches that matter most."
  - q: "How do you measure results?"
    a: "We track open rates, click-through rates, reply rates, conversion rates, and revenue attributed to each automation sequence. You get a monthly report showing exactly how many leads entered each workflow, how they progressed, and how many converted to customers. We continuously optimize based on this data."
